        <li class="lt-chem-349427">6 electrons; 3 orbitals</li>
        <li class="lt-chem-349427">10 electrons; 5 orbitals</li>
        <li class="lt-chem-349427">14 electrons; 7 orbitals</li>
    </ol>
    </div>
    </li>
    <li class="qandaentry lt-chem-349427" id="av_1.0-ch02_s05_s05_qs02_qd01_qa06_ans"> </li>
    <li class="qandaentry lt-chem-349427" id="av_1.0-ch02_s05_s05_qs02_qd01_qa07_ans">
    <div class="answer">
    <p class="para lt-chem-349427">A principal shell with <em>n</em> = 6 contains six subshells, with <em>l</em> = 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5, respectively. These subshells contain 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, and 11 orbitals, respectively, for a total of 36 orbitals. The energies of the orbitals with <em>n</em> = 6 are higher than those of the corresponding orbitals with the same value of <em>l</em> for <em>n</em> = 4.</p>
    </div>
    </li>
